Nine types do, six types don't.  But by type doesn't tell
enough of the story.  The third number in the table tells the
chance of random on the dungeon floor.

325 chances for,  335 chances against.  That moves closer to
what would appear in a game, but it does not take monster
initial inventories into account.

Priest, monk and wizard start with MC=3 cloaks, samurai with
MC=1 armor.  All other classes start with MC=0 armor.

Watchmen and soldiers get body armor that isn't too skewed
from the chances above.  Leather golems will skew the chances
towards favoring MC=0 leather armor.  Hobbits (elven mithril),
elves (elven mithril, elven cloak), dwarves (dwarvish mithril,
dwarvish cloak)and orcs (orcish chainmail, orcish cloak)
should about equal all the classes of soldier in an
extinctionist game.  But hobbits, elves, drawrves and orcs
outnumber soldiers in the mines for most of my games.

Since the mines deliver mithril, mithril's AC/weight ratio
beats any other armor until dragon mail, and both types of
mithril give MC=3, I think any combat wombat should end up
with MC=3 by the time they exit the mines.  Looking through
the above, dwarvish mithril in specific until enchant armor
scrolls get very common.  Spellcasters will be looking for
studden leather plus an MC=3 cloak until they get dragon
scales.



